Subject: [PATCH] build: derive package metadata version from the selected release
Origin: other, Peios catalogue qualification review
Upstream-Status: Pending [durable delegated recipe repair proposed upstream]

A packaging-only release tag may advance while the locked Rust crate version
stays unchanged. Use Pekit's selected immutable source release for package and
pkg-config metadata, retaining the Cargo manifest/lock, SONAME and ABI gates.

--- a/pekit.toml
+++ b/pekit.toml
@@ -71,8 +71,9 @@
 mkdir -p "$CARGO_HOME"
 cp "$PEKIT_VENDOR_OUT/cargo-config.toml" "$CARGO_HOME/config.toml"
 
-VERSION=$(sed -n 's/^version = "\([^"]*\)"/\1/p' Cargo.toml | head -1)
-test "$VERSION" = "$PEKIT_VERSION"
+# The selected immutable source release versions the package and pkg-config API.
+# Cargo keeps its own locked crate version; the C ABI remains SONAME .so.0.
+VERSION=${PEKIT_VERSION:?missing selected source release version}
 test -f "$PKM_UAPI/pkm/pkm.h"
 
 # Keep all source references independent of checkout and build-root paths.
